# Autoload Systems
- `EventBus`: global events (player/boss/combat/visual/audio). Emit instead of direct calls.
- `GameState`: lives, bombs, score, game flags, chain; emits changes.
- `EntityFactory`: pooling and safe creation; use it to spawn & cleanup entities.
- Template Managers: `EnemyTemplateManager`, `BossTemplateManager`, `StageTemplateManager`.

# Stage Flow
- `StageController` consumes `StageDefinition` + `WaveDefinition` and coordinates waves/boss.
- Spawns go through managers/factory; wave entries are safe dictionaries with defaults.

# Enemy/Boss Behaviors
- Component-based movement/attack (`MovementBehavior`, `AttackBehavior`, etc.).
- Boss phases are data-driven; apply behaviors directly (no racing with deferred adds).

# Integration Rules
- Never spawn scenes directly in random places; go via managers/factory.
- Keep events flowing through `EventBus`; don’t create new global singletons casually.
- Use safe defaults on missing data to avoid hard crashes.